Short:        UP-Term: XCON: console, vsh, tools
Author:       spotUP
Uploader:     UPLOADER-ADDRESS-PLACEHOLDER (spotUP)
Type:         comm/term
Version:      @VERSION@
Replaces:     PLACEHOLDER (the Aminet path of an earlier UP-Term upload, if there is one)
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 3.0.0; m68k-020
Requires:     AmigaOS 3.0 or newer, a 68020 or better
Distribution: Aminet

UP-Term is a console window for AmigaOS 3.x with a modern terminal inside (xterm,
Amiga and PC-ANSI dialects: 256 colours and RGB, scroll regions, alternate screen,
mouse, sixel images, UTF-8 with Unifont and emoji pages), a shell (vsh), GNU coreutils
and a set of Unix tools, the patched ixemul.library that Unix ports run on, and the
terminfo entry for TERM=vtcon.

This is the base archive. Neovim, Python, the Claude Code client and the pi coding
agent are separate archives; Neovim needs this one, the other three stand alone:
  comm/term/UP-Term-src.lha      source of the Unix tools and of coreutils (GPL)
  comm/misc/up-claude.lha           Claude Code client (stand-alone)
  comm/misc/up-pi.lha         pi coding agent (stand-alone)
  text/edit/up-nvim.lha     Neovim 0.12 (needs this archive)
  dev/lang/up-python.lha           Python 3.14 (stand-alone, brings its own ixemul.library)

Install: unpack, double-click Install (Installer 43 or newer). A second Install over an
installed UP-Term offers Update and leaves your settings alone. Uninstall removes it; it
asks before it removes UP-Term:var (sessions and history).

Licence: MIT (UP-Term's own code).
The parts it ships carry their own licences: LICENSES.txt in the archive lists each
part, its licence and where its source is.
